====================================================================================================
A5. Rotation law and the transport identity for S(h)
====================================================================================================
  c_(Rw) = c_w/2 (w_0 = 0) or (q c_w + G)/2 (w_0 = 1): exact on all 65476 words, q in {3,5}, p <= 14.
  S(h) = sum_w e(2^-j q^(k_j(w)) h c_w / M), k_j(w) = #ones among the first j letters: 2160 checks,
  max |difference| = 2.04e-12.  (So S(2^-j q^k h) = sum over words with k ones in their LAST j letters of
  e(h c/M) + the rest: a large archimedean coefficient at h is transported to the frequencies 2^-j q^k h.)

