C4. Archimedean part of the spectrum: S(h)/C at fixed theta = a/p (normalised DP) and the limit series
  dyadic (theta < log_3 2): x_w ~ Y = sum_n 3^n 2^(-D_n), D_n = position of the (n+1)-th one from the end;
  3-adic (theta > log_3 2): |x_w| ~ Z = sum_n 2^(sigma_n)/3^(n+1), sigma_n = position of the n-th one;
  letters iid Bernoulli(theta) in the limit; Monte Carlo with 2*10^5 samples, 160 terms (s.e. ~ 0.002).
==============================================================================================================
